<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69566" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶλῠ</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>moly</i>, a fabulous herb, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.305
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				641
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶλυς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in later
			writers, <i>garlic, Allium nigrum</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.15.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.47
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μώλυζα</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> a kind of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πήγανον ἄγριον</span> growing in Cappadocia, ib.<i><span class="en">
				46
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρύγγιον</span>
			, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρύχνον ὑπνωτικόν</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				21.180
			</span></i>. (Cf. Skt.<i>mū´lam</i> 'root',
				<i>mūlakarma</i> 'magical use of roots'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
